<title>BRAZIL: Breakdown of Tristao Brazil coffee crop estimate.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of Tristao Brazil coffee crop estimate.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian trade house Tristao has estimated Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop will reach 23.5 million 60-kg bags against an upwardly revised 1996/97 figure of 27.5 million bags.</p>
<p>A breakdown by state follows.</p>
<p>All figures are in '000 bags.</p>
<p> STATE						 1997/98</p>
<p>				Arabica     Conillon	 Total</p>
<p> SAO PAULO		    3,200			  3,200</p>
<p>    (Mogiana		  1,100			  1,100)</p>
<p>    (Rest		     2,100			  2,100)</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS		10,500	   100	 10,600</p>
<p>    (South		    5,100			  5,100)</p>
<p>    (Triangulo/west	 3,600			  3,600)</p>
<p>    (Zona da Mata/Capel.  1,800	   100	  1,900)</p>
<p> PARANA			 2,300			  2,300</p>
<p> ESPIRITO SANTO	     1,200	 2,900	  4,100</p>
<p> BAHIA			    750	   250	  1,000</p>
<p> RONDONIA			 100	 1,200	  1,300</p>
<p> OTHERS			   500	   500	  1,000</p>
<p> TOTAL			 18,550	 4,950	 23,500</p>
<p>A breakdown of the 1996/97 estimate by state follows.</p>
<p> STATE						 1996/97</p>
<p>			   Arabica     Conillon	 Total</p>
<p> SAO PAULO	     3,300			    3,300</p>
<p>    (Mogiana	   1,400			    1,400)</p>
<p>    (Rest		1,900			    1,900)</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS	  13,800			  13,800</p>
<p>    (South	     6,500			    6,500)</p>
<p>    (Triangulo/west  4,300			    4,300)</p>
<p>    (Zona da Mata    3,000			    3,000)</p>
<p> PARANA				1,500			  1,500</p>
<p> ESPIRITO SANTO		    1,900	 4,500	  6,400</p>
<p> BAHIA				   550	   150	    700</p>
<p> RONDONIA				100	   700	    800</p>
<p> OTHERS				  600	   400	  1,000</p>
<p> TOTAL				21,750	 5,750	 27,500</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
